Package: spmboost
Type: Package
Title: Model-Based Boosting with Gaussian Process Spatial Effects
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Lars", "Knieper", email = "lars.knieper@uni-goettingen.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Componentwise gradient boosting for point-referenced spatial
    data, extending 'mboost'. In every boosting iteration, a Gaussian process
    spatial effect is re-estimated by (restricted) maximum likelihood with
    'spmodel', and the base-learners are fitted to the residual after
    removing it. Predictions at new locations are obtained by kriging. A
    threshold on the spatial share of the residual variance allows the
    spatial effect to be dropped when it is negligible. Includes spatial and
    random cross-validation for choosing the number of boosting iterations.
URL: https://github.com/larsknieper/spmboost
BugReports: https://github.com/larsknieper/spmboost/issues
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0), mboost
Imports: spmodel, sf, spatialsample, parallel, stats, utils, graphics
License: GPL-2
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
